Chapter: CapLaunderPureMmio

 Probe (closed by capability stage 1b): memory-mapped device I/O has
 its own intrinsics - read-mmio and poke-mmio carry the Device.Mmio
 effect row, so a function with a pure signature cannot drive a
 device register through them. The heap intrinsics peek-byte and
 poke-byte stay pure by ruling (heap access is not I/O; the type
 system cannot tell a heap address from a device BAR at a runtime
 value, which is exactly why MMIO needs the dedicated intrinsics -
 see cap-heap-poke-pure for the sanctioned heap side). Here the
 effectful call cannot hide in a plain let (CDX2033) and the mmio
 effect is not declared in the signature (CDX2031).

Section: Definitions

  scribble-register : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  scribble-register (bar) (val) =
   let w = poke-mmio bar 0 val
   in read-mmio bar 0

  opening : Text = show (scribble-register 4160749568 1)

